@@ -1,8 +1,9 @@
 # Specializing enum conversion
 
-By default, enum values are serialized to JSON as integers. In some cases this could result in undesired behavior. If an
-enum is modified or re-ordered after data has been serialized to JSON, the later de-serialized JSON data may be
-undefined or a different enum value than was originally intended.
+By default, enum values are serialized to JSON as integers, preserving the signedness of the underlying type. Enums with
+unsigned underlying types are stored as unsigned integers. In some cases integer serialization could result in undesired
+behavior. If an enum is modified or re-ordered after data has been serialized to JSON, the later de-serialized JSON data
+may be undefined or a different enum value than was originally intended.
 
 It is possible to more precisely specify how a given enum is mapped to and from JSON as shown below:
 
